# Line endings are declared here rather than left to each machine's
# core.autocrlf. Without this file the endings in a working copy depend on a
# setting the repository cannot see, which is how an untouched file turns up as
# a whole-file diff on someone else's clone.
#
# `text=auto` stores LF in the repository and checks out whatever the platform
# uses, so Windows keeps CRLF locally and Linux keeps LF, and neither sees the
# other's endings in a diff.
* text=auto

# Never transformed, never diffed as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.webm binary
*.tif  binary
*.tiff binary
*.xisf binary
*.ser  binary
*.fits binary
*.fit  binary

# These are read by interpreters that care. A shell script with CRLF fails with
# `bad interpreter`, and PowerShell is happiest with CRLF.
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Resolved by uv, not written by hand: keep it out of diffs and out of the
# language statistics.
uv.lock linguist-generated=true

# Documentation, so the repository is not reported as mostly Markdown.
docs/*.md linguist-documentation=true
